Alkylation of MOF-bound triazolate (general procedure) and re-formation of $\mathbf{1}{\cdot}[\mathbf{Mn}(\mathbf{CO})_{3}(\mathbf{H}_{2}\mathbf{O})]\mathbf{Br}$ . Single crystals of $\mathbf{1\cdot}[\mathrm{Mn}(\mathrm{CO})_{3}(\mathrm{DMT})]$ , $\mathbf{1\cdot}[\mathrm{Mn}(\mathrm{CO})_{3}(\mathrm{ET})]$ , $\mathbf{1\cdot}[\mathrm{Mn}(\mathrm{CO})_{3}(\mathrm{HT})]$ , $\mathbf{1\cdot}[\mathrm{Mn}(\mathrm{CO})_{3}(\mathrm{OT})].$ and $\mathbf{1\cdot}[\mathrm{Mn}(\mathrm{CO})_{3}(\mathrm{DT})]$ (approx. $60\mathrm{mg}$ ) were washed with toluene $5\times10\mathrm{ml})$ followed by dichloromethane $(30\mathrm{ml})$ and $\mathrm{CDCl}_{3}$ $\mathrm{\nabla{\cdot}}5\mathrm{ml})$ ).  The sample was added to $\mathrm{CDCl}_{3}$ $(2~\mathrm{ml})$ in an $8~\mathrm{ml}$ glass vial with Teflon cap, degassed with Ar and cooled to $-10^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ in an ice-salt bath.  Simultaneously, MeBr was cooled to $-78^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ and an excess poured into the vial containing the MOF under flow of Ar.  The vial was sealed and heated to $50^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $20\mathrm{h}$ .  The sample was cooled to room temperature, the MOF crystals were isolated via filtration and washed with CDCl3 (5 ml) to yield $\mathbf{1}{\cdot}[\mathrm{Mn}(\mathrm{CO})_{3}(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O})]\mathrm{Br}$ as yellow single crystals. IR $\mathfrak{v}_{\mathrm{max}}$ (nujol, $\mathrm{cm^{-1}}$ ): 2040 (s, CO), 1951 (s, CO), 1921 (s, CO), 1606, 1553, 1510, 1493, 1408, 1305, 1272, 1182.
